{"id": "q0270", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 141.1, "n_chunks": 142, "n_concurrent": 142, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4714, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "B. Maximum flame temperature is 1,601°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 4.85 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas", "query": "A furnace operates with a gas inlet temperature of 650°C andan outlet temperature of 1,100°C. The inlet gas is composedof 10 percent CO, 20 percent CO_2 and 70 percent N_2 by volume.The combustion occurs with astoichiometric amountof air. Using the following data, determine the maximumflame temperature and the heat supplied to the furnacein Btu/ft^3 of exhaust gas. Data Standard heats of formation CO;\\DeltaH_f=- 26,400 cal/mole CO_2;\\DeltaH_f=- 94,050 cal/mole Heat capacities (cal deg^-1mole^-1) CO;C_p = 6.79 + 0.98 × 10^-3T - 0.11 × 10^5T^-2 O_2;C_p = 7.16 + 1.00 × 10^-3T - 0.40 × 10^5T^-2 CO_2;C_p = 10.55 + 2.16 × 10^-3T - 2.04 × 10^5T^-2 N_2;C_p = 6.66 + 1.02 × 10^-3T Combustion reaction 2CO_(_g)_ + O_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2CO_2(g)\n\nA. Maximum flame temperature is 1,750°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 4.5 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nB. Maximum flame temperature is 1,601°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 4.85 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nC. Maximum flame temperature is 1,650°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 5.2 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nD. Maximum flame temperature is 1,500°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 5.5 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nE. Maximum flame temperature is 1,550°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 4.2 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nF. Maximum flame temperature is 1,800°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 3.9 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nG. Maximum flame temperature is 1,450°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 5.8 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nH. Maximum flame temperature is 1,800°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 5.0 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nI. Maximum flame temperature is 1,701°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 4.7 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\nJ. Maximum flame temperature is 1,700°C, Heat supplied to the furnace is 4.0 Btu/ft^3 exhaust gas\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "furnace operates with a gas inlet temperature of 650 degrees and outlet temperature of 1100 degrees. The inlet gas is composed of 10 percent CO, 20 percent CO2, and 70 percent N2 by volume. The combustion occurs with a stoichiometric amount of air. Using the following data, determine the maximum flame temperature and the heat supplied to the furnace in BTU/ft^3 of exhaust gas. Data: Standard heats of formation: CO, ΔHf = -26,400 cal/mol; CO2, ΔHf = -94,000 cal/mol. Heat capacities: CO, Cp = 6.79 + 0.998 x 10^-3 T (cal/mol-deg); CO2, Cp = 10.55 + 2.16 x 10^-3 T - 2.04 x 10^-5 T^2 (cal/mol-deg); N2, Cp = 6.66 - 1.02 x 10^-3 T (cal/mol-deg). Combustion reaction: 2CO(g) + O2(g) --> 2CO2(g). A) Maximum flame temperature is 1750 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 4.5 BTU/ft^3 exhaust gas. B) Maximum flame temperature is 1601 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 4.85 BTU/ft^3 exhaust gas. C) Maximum flame temperature is 1650 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 5.2 BTU/ft^3 exhaust gas. D) Maximum flame temperature is 1500 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 5.5 BTU/ft^3 exhaust gas. E) Maximum flame temperature is 1550 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 4.2 BTU/ft^3 exhaust gas. F) Maximum flame temperature is 1800 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 3.9 BTU/ft^3 exhaust gas. G) Maximum flame temperature is 1400 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 5.8 BTU/ft^3 exhaust gas. H) Maximum flame temperature is 1800 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 5.0 BT", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Based on the calculations, the maximum flame temperature reached 1601 degrees, and the heat supplied to the furnace was 4.85 BTU per cubic foot of exhaust gas.", "expert_answer": "B) Maximum flame temperature is 1601 degrees; heat supplied to the furnace is 4.85 BTU/ft³ exhaust gas.", "expert_latency_s": 9.97, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 867}
{"id": "q0279", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 35.74, "n_chunks": 36, "n_concurrent": 36, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.455, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "E. 1819 ft/sec", "query": "Using the steam tables, calculate the velocity in a nozzle at a pointwhere the pressure is 40Psiawhen the superheated steamflows from a boiler. The initial boiler conditions are P(pressure) = 80Psia, T(temperature) = 500°F, and V(velocity) = 0.\n\nA. 2100 ft/sec\nB. 2200 ft/sec\nC. 1500 ft/sec\nD. 1950 ft/sec\nE. 1819 ft/sec\nF. 1600 ft/sec\nG. 1900 ft/sec\nH. 1700 ft/sec\nI. 2000 ft/sec\nJ. 1400 ft/sec\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "Using the steam tables, calculate the velocity in a nozzle at a point where the pressure is forty (40) psia when the superheated steam flows from a boiler. The initial boiler conditions are P (pressure) equals eighty (80) psia, T (temperature) equals five hundred (500) degrees Fahrenheit, and V (velocity) equals zero (0). A) twenty-one hundred (2100) ft/sec B) twenty-two hundred (2200) ft/sec C) fifteen hundred (1500) ft/sec D) fifty (50) ft/sec E) nineteen hundred (1900) ft/sec F) sixteen hundred (1600) ft/sec G) nineteen hundred (1900) ft/sec H) seventeen hundred (1700) ft/sec I) two thousand (2000) ft/sec J) fourteen hundred (1400) ft/sec. Answer with the correct option letter and its content.", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The correct answer is E, nineteen hundred ft/sec.", "expert_answer": "E) nineteen hundred (1900) ft/sec", "expert_latency_s": 9.58, "stall_ms": 24, "relay_ms": 289}
{"id": "q0297", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 14.6, "n_chunks": 15, "n_concurrent": 15, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3637, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": "F. 1", "query": "Let l = [1,2,3,4]. What is min(l) in Python3?\n\nA. '1'\nB. 0\nC. -1\nD. 3\nE. [1,2,3,4]\nF. 1\nG. 2\nH. min(l) is not defined in Python3\nI. 4\nJ. 1.0\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "Answer: B) 0", "mode": "local", "answer": "Answer is B. 0. The min function returns the smallest item in an iterable or the smallest of two or more arguments. In the list [1, 3, 4], the smallest number is 1. So min-l is 1.", "answer_ms": 1231}
