{"id": "q0456", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.82, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0586, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "How can I sleep well at night?", "transcript": "How can I sleep well at night?", "mode": "local", "answer": "To sleep well at night, try to stick to a regular sleep schedule by going to bed and waking up at the same time every day. Create a calming bedtime routine, like reading or taking a warm bath. Make your bedroom comfortable—keep it cool, dark, and quiet. Limit screen time before bed, as the blue light can interfere with sleep. Avoid caffeine and heavy meals close to bedtime. If you're still having trouble, consider talking to a healthcare provider.", "answer_ms": 2209}
{"id": "q0462", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.25, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1846, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the best watch in the world ?", "transcript": "What is the best watch in the world?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The best watch in the world depends on what you mean by \"best.\" If you're looking for luxury and prestige, many would say the Patek Philippe Calatrava is the ultimate classic. For technical innovation, the Apple Watch Series 9 or Rolex Submariner might be top contenders. If you love unique craftsmanship, independent brands like MB & F or Urwerk offer incredible artistry. What matters most to you—style, technology, heritage, or something else?", "answer_ms": 2309}
